  "necessity_paragraph": "The patient presents with recurrent episodes of palpitations and lightheadedness, raising concern for paroxysmal atrial fibrillation in the context of a personal history of transient ischemic attacks and cerebral infarction. To evaluate for potential arrhythmic causes of these transient cerebral ischemic events and guide anticoagulation management, a cardiac event monitoring study (CPT 93271) is ordered. This service is supported by the clinical indication note, which documents the palpitations, lightheadedness, and history of transient ischemic attacks and cerebral infarction, along with the stated purpose of evaluating arrhythmic causes and guiding anticoagulation management."
